From 6963477deb3d8acf4e6f67c50d66355317858903 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:49:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Linear solver override

The option --linear-solver-override (-lso, declared by
declareDefaultOptions) or else the environment variable
MFEM_MGIS_LINEAR_SOLVER_OVERRIDE, read by mfem_mgis::initialize, gives a
linear solver which replaces the linear solvers set by the setLinearSolver
methods of all the non linear evolution problems, by name and parameters
or by a linear solver built by the program. It is described as the
preconditioners of the linear solvers: a name, or a map with the entries
Name and Options, in the syntax of the data of TFEL, for instance
{Name: "BelosSolver", Options: {Solver: "CG", Preconditioner: {Name:
"MueLu"}}}, converted to parameters (integers, reals, strings, booleans,
lists, maps, empty braces). The first replacement is reported on the
output of MFEM; a linear solver override which can't be built is reported
as such. It allows the comparison of linear solvers on existing programs
without recompiling them. The linear solvers built by the non linear
solvers from their own parameters (fixed point solver) and those of PETSc
(--use-petsc) are not replaced.

The option given twice or without value, an invalid description, and
different descriptions on the processes of MPI are refused by
mfem_mgis::initialize. The description is read by the utilities of TFEL
(tfel::TFELUtilities, linked privately, found by the installed
configuration for the projects using the static library, in the TFEL of
MGIS first); without them, a linear solver override is refused.

Tests: TwoLayerCube, which requests GMRESSolver, with a conjugate gradient
given by the variable (sequential) and by the option with a preconditioner
whose options are empty braces (2 processes): the replacement is reported
and the solution is checked; an invalid description and the option given
twice are refused (ExecutionSettingsTest). Checked by hand: the linear
solver built by the program (StationaryNonLinearHeatTransferTest) is
replaced.
